# UI rules

## Layout

Phone first. Design at 375px, then widen. The old version had eight wrapping
tabs — do not recreate them. Navigation is a fixed bottom bar with four items:
الحروف · الكلمات · التدريب · عن الموقع.

## Coptic and Arabic together

`<html dir="rtl" lang="ar">`. Any Coptic or Latin string inside Arabic text is
wrapped so it cannot flip the line:

```tsx
<span dir="ltr" className="inline-block">{letter.unicode.upper}</span>
```

Coptic glyphs are the largest thing on any page. Arabic is the reading language.
English, when present, is one small line — never a parallel column.

## The seven group colors

They are pedagogy, not decoration — a learner recognises "group 4 letters" by
color. Defined once as CSS custom properties `--group-1` … `--group-7` and used
through Tailwind tokens. Never hardcode a hex in a component. Every group color
must pass 4.5:1 against its own text color in both themes; if one fails, adjust
the token and say which.

## Interaction

Expanding panels, not CSS 3D flips. The old 450px flip cards were slow on
phones and invisible to screen readers. A panel:

- is a real `<button>` with `aria-expanded`
- animates height and opacity only, and respects `prefers-reduced-motion`
- keeps the glyph visible while the back content opens

Audio buttons are labelled in Arabic (`aria-label="استمع"`), never an icon alone.

## Things that were broken in the old version — do not repeat

- invalid CSS: `space-y` as a property, a gradient used as a border color
- dark-mode header text bound to a variable that resolves to dark gray
- tab lists without `role="tablist"` / `aria-selected`
- Google Fonts loaded by `<link>` while Coptic was local — use `next/font`
  for both, self-hosted
